# Compiled compiler binary — any depth, not just the repo root: the direct
# g++ build (./aster), a CMake -B build dir, a suite OUT dir, or a nested
# project's build output (tests/ci.sh also copies it to $PWD/aster).
**/aster
# Per-project build cache (aster build writes <proj>/build/.cache/*.meta and
# *.so): the cache lives under the project, so this must match at any depth,
# not just the repo root.
**/build/
/tmp-*
# v0.23.64-dev: tests/ci.sh writes aster.tmp.$$ and renames it; an interrupted
# run leaves the temporary behind, and **/aster above does not match it.
*.tmp.*
*.o
*.so
*.elf
*.apk
# Static archives and compiler dependency files. No current producer in-tree
# emits either (no ar/-MMD invocation found); added per audit §6.2 so a
# future producer cannot leak build products into the tree.
*.a
*.d

# v0.23.71-dev: these four are committed reference fixtures, not build
# products. The generic *.o / *.so rules above would otherwise hide them and
# a fresh checkout would have no frozen symtab snapshot to compare against.
!tests/baseline/symtab-frozen/*.o
!tests/baseline/symtab-frozen/*.so

# Coredumps / debug artifacts
core
core.*
*.core
qemu_deep.bin_*

# Coverage products (tests/coverage-checks.sh builds with --coverage and
# runs gcov; the .gcno/.gcda land in its OUT dir and the .gcov next to them).
# That OUT dir itself (tmp-coverage-checks) is already covered by /tmp-*.
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov

# Logs
build.log
*.log
/ci-artifacts/
# v0.23.81-dev: bootstrap-loop-checks.sh writes OUT=bootstrap-loop-artifacts
# and self-cleans via an EXIT trap, but a SIGKILL/timeout kill leaves it
# behind; the "working tree clean" CI step would then fail on residue.
# (Its OUT dir does not carry a tmp- prefix, so /tmp-* does not cover it.)
/bootstrap-loop-artifacts/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local keystore (RSA private key) — never commit. The keystore is per
# project (<proj>/.aster/), so this must match at any depth, not just the
# repo root (a nested .aster/ was already observed under ci-artifacts/keys/).
**/.aster/

# Editor / IDE and OS files — none of these are currently in the tree;
# preventive, per audit §6.2. (.idea/ is plausible: CMakeLists.txt exists
# as an editor/IDE aid. No Windows-only entries: nothing in the repo
# produces desktop.ini.)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
